# Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request" above a request).
# Start the server first: uvicorn app.main:app --reload
# "owner" is an event owner (OWNER_IDS), any other id is a normal user.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Create an event (owner)
POST {{base}}/events
X-User-Id: owner
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Event1",
  "availableTickets": 400,
  "eventDate": "2123-01-04T20:00:00Z"
}

### List upcoming events (any user)
GET {{base}}/events
X-User-Id: alice

### Book 2 tickets for event 1
POST {{base}}/events/1/tickets
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2 }

### Book 1 ticket (body is optional, quantity defaults to 1)
POST {{base}}/events/1/tickets
X-User-Id: bob

### My tickets
GET {{base}}/tickets
X-User-Id: alice

### Ticket numbers for event 1 (owner of that event)
GET {{base}}/events/1/stats
X-User-Id: owner

### Cancel event 1 (owner of that event, safe to repeat)
DELETE {{base}}/events/1
X-User-Id: owner

### Error: no X-User-Id -> 401 problem+json
GET {{base}}/events

### Error: normal user creates an event -> 403
POST {{base}}/events
X-User-Id: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nope", "availableTickets": 10, "eventDate": "2123-01-04T20:00:00Z" }

### Error: invalid body -> 400 with a list of field errors
POST {{base}}/events
X-User-Id: owner
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Broken", "availableTickets": "many" }
